# Normalize line endings in the repository to LF.
#
# Without this the repo drifts: some files were committed with CRLF and some
# with LF, so any tool that rewrites a whole file (a formatter, an editor with
# different settings, a script) silently flips every line and turns a two-line
# change into a thousand-line diff.
#
# Git stores LF and checks out the platform's native endings, so this changes
# nothing about how the files look on a Windows machine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets git must never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.xlsx binary
*.db binary
